From 7c8e3114587909f35faa232d7edfd73cb28d9526 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arch-port <26345330+DrShadow34@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:03:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] panvk: v9 compressed images U-interleaved, copies by
 blocks

Images with a compressed format and transfer usage got MUTABLE_FORMAT |
BLOCK_TEXEL_VIEW_COMPATIBLE from panvk itself, for vk_meta's copies
through RGBA32UI / RG32UI views, and that rules out U-interleaved
tiling: compressed formats tile in 4x4 blocks, uncompressed ones in
16x16 texels, so no uncompressed view can alias the layout. Every BC /
ETC2 / ASTC texture a D3D game uploads (DXVK: TRANSFER_SRC | DST |
SAMPLED) was LINEAR; Risk of Rain 2 had ~2700 of them.

On v9 such images no longer get the flags (unless the app asks for
uncompressed views, or the image ends up LINEAR anyway) and every copy
touching a compressed U-interleaved image (buffer <-> image, image <->
image, compressed <-> size-compatible uncompressed, 2D arrays and 3D)
goes through panlib_copy_image_blocks, a libpan kernel computing the
tiled addresses itself (one invocation per 8 / 16 byte block, linear,
4x4 or 16x16 U-interleaved on either side). Host image copies already
handle compressed U-interleaved images on the CPU.

CTS (texture.compressed, copy_and_blit image_to_buffer / buffer_to_image
2D + 3D, image_to_image all_formats 1/3, blit_image all_formats with
compressed sources 1/25, image.texel_view_compatible 1/4): 6769 pass,
0 fail. Risk of Rain 2 main menu (1080x2160, GPU bound): ~3% less GPU
time per pass; texture reads there are dominated by RGBA16F targets and
a 4096^2 shadow map.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013fD3if93WntovhmD8fGa8C
